      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1914-05-23_WidnesExaminer_art0005" n="art0005">
        <p>22nd May. 1914. • COUNTY BOROTiGII OF WARRINGTON. TO PAINTERS AND DECORATORS. The Sites and Buildings Committee of the Education Committee of the Council of the County Borough of Warrington is prepared to receive TENDERS for the PAINTING of the various Schools. Specifications, forms of tender and all further information may be obtained at the Office of the Borough Surveyor, Town Hall, on and after Wednesday next, the 27th inst., at which place tenders must be delivered before 12 o'clock noon on Thursday, the 11th day of June, 1914. A deposit of 1016 will be required for the Specification, which sum will be returned on receipt of a bona-fide tender. Cheques to be made payable to the Borough Treasurer. The lowest or any tender not necessarily accepted. ANDREW M. KER, Borough Engineer &amp; Surveyor Borough Engineer &amp; Surveyor's Office, May 22nd, 1914.</p>
      </div>
