      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1914-05-23_WidnesExaminer_art0010" n="art0010">
        <p>Town Nall. Warrington.</p>
        <p>RUNCORN UNION. ASSISTANT NURSE. An Assistant Nurse (to take alternate day and night duty) is Required at the Workhouse at Dutton, near Warrington. Salary, £25 per annum, with uniform, board, washing, and lodgings in the Nurses' Home within the Workhouse precincts. Candidates must have received some training in general nursing, and the appointment will be subject to the approval of the Local Gov- ernment Board. Applications, stating age, experience, and whether single or widow, accompanied by copies of not more than two recent testimonials, must reach my Office, 71, High-street, Runcorn, not later than Ten o'clock on Wednesday morning, the 3rd day of June, 1914. Any further information may be obtained from the Matron of the Workhouse. GEO. F. ASHTON, Clerk to the _Guardians. Union Offices, Runcorn, 20th May, 1914..</p>
