        <head>WEDNESDAY.</head>
        <p>WEDNESDAY.</p>
        <p>Before Messrs. S. R. Armitage (in the chair), C. Parr, J. Bailey, J. Ball and W. Fumes!</p>
        <p>Street Betting.—Edwin Scott was fined ° and costs, with an alternative of two niolit imprisonment for loitering in Earle-Stil Earlestown, for the purpose of receiving be,tl When arrested he endeavoured to dispose 01, slips by putting them into his mouth and 011, ing them. He was not successful, for Detecl; Mullen found other slips on the defendaw Defendant had been previously convicted.</p>
        <p>Thrown Out of a Sidecar.—James Ranq Rigby-street, St. Helens, was charged with ing been drunk and disorderly and with cal grievous bodily harm to Mrs. Mary Ws' wife of a Leigh stockbroker. On MondaY Walker was out with his wife and child 1), motor cycle and sidecar. In Ashton-road, ton-le-Willows, prisoner was with a numb° men who were more or less drunk. prise went in the middle of the road and waved arms about in front of the vehicle. In his, deavour to negotiate the prisoner and a CO Mr. Walker was unsuccessful, with the-r— _</p>
