        <head>AMATEUR ASSOCIATION.</head>
        <p>AMATEUR ASSOCIATION.</p>
        <p>FIRST ROUND.</p>
        <p>We have only received full particulars of two of the matches in this competition, and in the appended results the ?lame of the member of the winning team is printed first in each case : Crosfield's (NO. 2) v. Fearnhead. Played at Crosfield's. Crosfield's (No. 2) won by 33 points.</p>
        <p>S. Adams, 21; James Robert, 17. A. Middleton, 21; John Smith, 11. A. Cooper, 21; John Weston, 18. J. Archer, 21; J. Bradshaw, 6. . W. Whatmough, 14; J. Hewitt, 21. R. Ritchie, 18; J. Hardman, 21. J. Woodward, 21; Jos. Weston, 10. Total—Crosfield's (No. 2), 137; Fearnhead, 104.</p>
        <p>Played at Fearnhead. Fearnhead won by 82 points. P. Croughton, 21; J. Ashburner, 18. W. Goulden, 21; H. Bishop, 18. H. Ratcliffe, 21; E. Warburton, 6. W. Weston, 21; W. Lawton, 6. J. Holcroft, 21; J. Oakes, 6. F. Weston, 21; S. Taylor, 5. T. Bond, 21; W. Howard, 6. Total—Fearnhead, 147; Crosfield's (No. 2), 65. On the home-and-home matches Fearnhead won by 49 points. Penketh v. Junior Conservatives. Penketh had to bow the knee to the Conserva- tives, losing on the total by 45 points. The match at Penketh proved the most exciting, some hard, close games taking place. W. Shave (capt.), R. Gregson, and E. Ashton, were the pick of the team in the order named. The away match was a failure, Penketh find- ing the green very easy running and very hard to play on. The scores were : At Penketh. Penketh won by 18 points.</p>
