        <head>SWIMMING.</head>
        <p>SWIMMING.</p>
        <p>LOCAL CLUB'S ACTIVITIES.</p>
        <p>The Warrington Swimming Club commence their season next Thursday at 8.15 p.m. with a water f)olo match versus Runcorn, in connec- tion with the Liverpool and District League (Division II.). The Warrington team will be chosen from the following players: Woods, Jolley, L. Graham, Ince, Sutton, Sisson, Pepper, J. Graham, and C. Turner (captain). A good game is expected, as Runcorn have nOt been beaten this season. Their team will include H. Beaman, a well-known local swimmer. Also on the same night the first round of the Inter- Works Squadron Handicap Race will take place as follows: Corporation Tramways V. Co-opera- tpi .v ea nSdt oKr s (No. eve. r co srso svie ild),oss twOoffi c2e) (pNroi v. alt)e, Traders v. Forshaw and Sons. All spectators are assured a good entertainment.</p>
      </div>
