        <head>, LAWN TENNIS.</head>
        <p>, LAWN TENNIS.</p>
        <p>"CAUSEWAY" v. PADGATE. Played at Wilderspool on Saturday. Results: Ladies' Doubles.—Mrs. H. Hope and Miss Wilson beat Mrs. Sherburn and Miss B. Eng- land, 6-4, 6--3; Mrs. S. Woods and Mrs. Green lost to Miss England and Mrs. J. Burn, 2-6, 1-6; Miss D. Isaac and Miss G. Wilson beat Miss Walker and Miss Lunt, 6-5, 6-4. Gent's Doubles.—Messrs. W. Woods and J. Paterson beat Messrs. H. B. Nicholson and S. Duckworth, 6-1, 6-5; Messrs. S. Woods and R. Walsh beat Messrs. C. R. Chambers and W. H. Houghton, 6-4, 4-6, 6-2; Messrs. H. Hope and H. Bibby beat W. G. Wood and J. Burn, 6-5, 6-3.</p>
        <p>_ Mixed Doubles.—Mr. S. Woods and Miss Wil- son lost to Mr. H. B. Nicholson and Mrs. Sher- burn, 6-3, 3-6, 2-6; Mr. and Mrs. H. Hope lost to Mr. P. Duckworth and Miss B. England, 6-4, 4-6, 4-6; Mr. W. Woods and Mrs. S. Woods lost to Mr. C. R. Chambers and Miss England, 5-6, 5-6; Mr. J. Paterson and Mrs. Green lost to Mr. W. H. Houghton and Mrs. J. Burn, 4-6, 6-5, 0-6; Mr. H. Bibby and Miss D. Isaac beat Mr. W. G. Wood and Miss Walker, 6-4. 4-6, 6-1; Mr. R. Walsh and Miss G. Wil- son beat Mr. J. Burn and Miss Lunt, 6-2, 2-6, 6-2.</p>
        <p>Result: " Causeway " won 7 events to 5; 17 sets to 13; and 142 games to 135.</p>
        <p>"CAUSEWAY" 11. v. PADGATE 11. At Padgate. Result: Padgate won 9 events to 3; 19 sets to 10; 152 game's to 113.</p>
