        <p>lATEEKLY CONDUCTED PARTIES TO V V CANADA.—Choice of finest, fastest, cheapest boats. Up-to-date, disinterested advice free. Work guaranteed in Canada (men and women). To ordinary second and third class passengers THE SALVATION ARMY ORGANISED EMIGRATION SHIPPING DEPARTMENT offers advantages here and in Canada, U.S.A., Australia, New Zealand, etc., avhich no other organisation possesses. Write or all, Commissioner Lamb, 122, Queen Victoria- street, London; or 170 a, London-road, Liverpool. COUNTY BOROUGH OF WARRINGTON. SHOPS ACT, 1912. NOTICE IS HEREBY GIVEN that the Council on application made to them propose to make an Order for the undermentioned area fixing the day of the weekly half-holiday and the closing hours for the trades hereinafter mentioned as follows : NAME OF TRADES. DRAPERS, CLOTHIERS, TAILORS, HATTERS and OUTFITTERS. DAY OF WEEKLY HALF-ROLIDAY. THURSDAY, 1 P.M. (Or, at the option of Shopkeeper, Saturday.) CLOSING HOURS: MONDAY, 8 p.m. WEDNESDAY, 8 p.m. TUESDAY, 7.30 p.m. FRIDAY, 8.30 p.m. SATURDAY, 10.30 P.M. provided that the Order shall be suspended for the seven days immediately preceding Good Friday, Whit Monday, Warrington "Walking Day, August Bank Holiday, and Christmas Day respectively, and provided also that where the occupier of a shop elects to close his shop for the weekly half-holiday on Saturday instead of on Thursday, the closing hour on Thursday shall be 7.30 p.m. AREA: All streets and other public places in the , centre of the Borough being within the • area bounded by and including the follow- ing streets: Crosfield-street, Parker-street, Wilson-Patten-street, Arpley-road, Bridge- street, Mersey-street, Howard-place, Butter- market-street, Scotland-road, Horsemarket- street, Winwick-street to Winwick-road, , Tanners-lane, Bewsey-street, Frogh all-lane to Crosfield-street. Any 'person wishing to make objection to the Order or suggestions as to the provisions of the Order should address a statement in writing to the undersigned before the 17th day of June next. NOTICE IS ALSO HEREBY GIVEN that the occupier of any shop to be affected by the Order may, on presenting himself at the Health Office, Garven House, Sankey-street, during office hours, on any day before the aforesaid date, verify that his name, address and trade are duly entered in the Register of Shops. Dated this 15th day of May. 1914. J. LYON WHITTLE, Town Clerk. Town Hall, Warrington.</p>
