        <p>4ANCASHIRE COUNTY ASYLUM, WINWICK, WARRINGTON. The Committee of Visitors invite TENDERS for the Supply of HOUSE COAL from the Ist July, 1914, for a period of three, six or twelve months. Tenders must be made upon forms which can be obtained on application being made to the undersigned, and must be delivered at the Asylum not later than 9 a.m. on Wednesday, the 10th June, addressed The Chairman of the Visiting Committee, and endorsed " Tender for House Coal." Application for Tender Forms must be addressed " The Clerk and Steward, Lancashire County Asylum, Winwick, Warring- ton." The Committee do not bind themselves to accept the lowest or any tender, and reserve to themselves the right to accept or reject the whole or part of any Tender. By order, P. IRVING DUTTON, Clerk and Steward.</p>
