        <p>COUNTY BOROUGH OF WARRINGTON. TO CONTRACTOR'S MERCHANTS, QUARRY OWNERS, AND EARTHENWARE PIPE MANUFACTURERS. The Paving and Sewerage Committee of the Council of the County Borough of Warrington is prepared to receive TENDERS for 400 TONS of TARRED MACADAM and 1,100 YARDS of 18-inch STONEWARE PIPES. Spe,cifications, forms of tender 'and all further , information may be obtained at the Office of the Borough Surveyor, Town Hall, on and after Wednesday, the 27th inst., at which place tenders must be delivered before 12 o'clock mon 1 on Monday, the Bth day of June, 1914. The lowest or any tender not necessarily accepted. ANDREW M. KER, Borough Engineer &amp; Surveyor Borough Engineer &amp; Surveyor's Office, May 22nd, 1914.</p>
        <p>Appointments by Public Authorities. COUNTY BOROUGH OF WARRINGTON. JUNIOR CLERKSHIPS IN CORPORA- TION DEPARTMENTS. An EXAMINATION for the purpose of form- ing a "Waiting List" for appointments to Junior Clerkships in Corporation Offices during the twelve months commencing Ist August, 1914, will be held in the month of June next. Vacan- cies, not filled by promotion, occurring after the date mentioned, will be filled from the Waiting List" of Candidates who have obtained not less than 60 per cent, of marks. Before appoint- ment Candidates will be required to submit themselves to an Examination by the Medical Officer of Health. Candidates obtaining not less than 60 per cent. of marks will be furnished with a certificate to that effect. Applicants must be the sons of ratepayers of the Borough, and must not be less than 14 or more than 15i years of age on the Ist August, •1914. Forms of application may be obtained from the Town Clerk's Office, and no Candidate will be admitted for examination unless he has re- turned the form, duly completed, not later than noon on Monday, the first day of June, 1914. Dated this 15th day of May, 1914. J. LYON WHITTLE. Town Clerk.</p>
